The x86 decider of the tcalc lane (backend x86-flat): copies, never edited here.

Origin: Mettapedia/MettaKernel/tcalc-compiled (the compiled tcalc artifacts),
copied one way by `make tcalc-x86-sync`, which refuses a checksum mismatch.

  ordinary_flat_cesta_runtime.S    the runtime image: four functions, each an
                                   .incbin slice of the linked bytes below
  ordinary_flat_cesta_linked.text  the exact linked bytes (1,447): flat_fire
                                   0+211, ordinary_flat_pack 211+530,
                                   ordinary_flat_adapter 741+704,
                                   ordinary_flat_failure 1445+2
  ordinary_flat_cesta.h            the adapter's ABI, generated by Cesta

What is proved (HOL Light, against the s2n-bignum x86 model, in the origin's
proofs/): flat_fire, the 211-byte leaf, is correct (FLAT_FIRE_CORRECT and its
traced and full-workspace forms); the adapter's mathematical outputs keep the
meaning of an ordinary-row firing. Not proved: the machine code of
ordinary_flat_pack and ordinary_flat_adapter (that proof is paused). A firing
decided through this image is therefore decided by a proved leaf behind an
unproved packing adapter.

`make tcalc-x86-check` compares each function's bytes in the linked cetta
binary with its slice of ordinary_flat_cesta_linked.text.

